module gunbc.rung_drop.v1_required_lanes_withdrawn

import std.types { List, NonEmptyStr, String }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, ReplacementStaged }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }

// DECLARED 2026-10-09 ON AN OPERATOR RULING (the brief to session smart-gull-336, the v2 half of the
// v1 withdrawal): "v1 is effectively bankrupt due to memory instability - i want to go back to pure
// v2 native compiler development - that means deleting most of our current CI jobs", and "i suggest
// we bankrupt the current CI first". The change that carries this row deletes four of the five lanes
// the required context read -- `floor`, `generated`, `rust-unit-tests` and `seed` -- from
// gunbc.compiler_gate_workflow and leaves the emit-and-build steps as the one required job,
// `witnesses` (the same ruling collapsed `emit-build` and the aggregate that read it into that job,
// and requires it to emit and build both products fresh on every run).
//
// WHY THE LANES ARE DELETED AND NOT GIVEN HEADROOM. The floor already ran at its slot's throttle
// line (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode required_floor_runs_at_its_memory_ceiling carries that receipt),
// and every repair on offer -- a larger slot, an allocator setting, a narrower subject -- spends work
// on the interpreter the ruling retires. The ruling withdraws v1 as a validation authority; it does
// not ask for a cheaper v1 gate.
//
// THIS IS A DROP AND NOT A CLEAN-UP, WHICH IS WHY IT IS ONE ROW WITH A WIDE POPULATION. Nothing the
// four lanes held is held by anything else today. The surviving job establishes that the seed emits
// two v2 closures and that the emitted crates build and start, and a green required context says
// that and nothing more.
//
// WHAT THIS ROW DOES NOT DO. It does not amend the rows that already described losses on these lanes
// (required_gate_bankruptcy, witness_floor_off_the_required_gate,
// required_lanes_do_not_resolve_product_layer_modules, v1_integration_tests_deleted_from_the_unit_lane
// and their neighbours). Their triggers name capabilities, and a native lane can still fire them. The
// one row this change does supersede is rust_unit_tests_off_pull_requests, whose own text says the
// unit lane still blocks at the merge queue; it no longer runs anywhere.

data v1_required_lanes_withdrawn_population: List<String> = [
  "every claim the `floor` lane folded on a pull request or a merge_group: the prepared subject of `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes` with its seeds, plus the changed-witness and touched-entry selection. `claim_executor --required-ci --required-lane witnesses` is run by no job",
  "the stage0 mirrors equal one emission by the seed built from them, and the registry-rostered generated artifacts (`gunbc.generated_artifact_registry` `committed_generated_artifacts`) equal one emission of their authorities: `claim_executor --required-ci --required-lane build` is run by no job. That population includes `.github/workflows/witnesses.yml` and `DESIGN.md`, so the gate's own workflow file is compared with `gunbc.compiler_gate_workflow` by nothing; the heal publisher workflow that published repair candidates was deleted with the lanes (nothing sealed one), and its WIF pool (`gunbc.auth.heal_publisher_federation`) stands dead until retired by hand -- an external-estate obligation, not a drop",
  "the lint: `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` (`gunbc.repo_self_build` `repo_self_clippy_command`), the only command that compiles the integration-test and example targets",
  "the v1 unit tests: `cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib` (`gunbc.repo_self_build` `repo_self_test_command`), which ran on merge_group and workflow_dispatch",
  "module resolution: every module the source-root ingestion admits under dag/ and src/v2/ that is outside the import closures of `gunbc.instrument_targets` `self_host_entry` and `v2_native_cli_entry` is handed to a compiler by no required step, so it can stop resolving on main with the required context green. Enumerated BY IDENTITY, not by count, by `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:required-lane-resolution-census` (`gunbc.required_lane_resolution_census_live`), which from this change does not hold by design",
  "the consumers of those lanes' products: no merge_group run uploads a compiler pair candidate. Fleet-desired admission, which used to build that pair and advance `refs/fleet/desired`, is withdrawn: the admitted revision is what has landed on `origin/main`. `gunbc.fleet_revision_acceptance` still names a required-CI success that carries the `witnesses` job's emit-and-build verdict, under the contract epoch `gunbc.required_ci_contract_epoch` moved to with the lane withdrawal, and is not the production admission path",
  "NOT ENUMERATED HERE, and named so the gap is not read as empty: every `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` row and every standing `gunbc.rung_drop` row whose stated current rung is held by a step of the four lanes. Those rows are not amended by this change, and each now sits no higher than this row's temporary rung",
]

data v1_required_lanes_withdrawn: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "v1_required_lanes_withdrawn" as NonEmptyStr,
  subject: "The four v1-judged required lanes (`floor`, `generated`, `rust-unit-tests`, `seed`) as a merge gate",
  declared: "2026-10-09",
  standing: Standing,
  declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: ReplacementStaged {
      replacement: "a binary built from an emission of v2 judging this population on the required path, admitted to the gate as rows of `gunbc.emitted_subject_build_gate` `emitted_subject_build_rows`. No such row covers any member of this population at declaration"
    },
    population: v1_required_lanes_withdrawn_population,
    restoration_trigger: "THE CAPABILITY: on every landing revision, a binary built from an emission of v2 -- the seed's emission today, v2's own after the generation transition -- judges this population on the required path with a discriminating red. Member by member: (1) every claim the floor folded is executed by such a binary, or its subject has been deleted; (2) every module the source-root ingestion admits is resolved, observed as `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:required-lane-resolution-census` holding against the workflow as emitted; (3) every committed generated artifact, `.github/workflows/witnesses.yml` included, is compared with one emission of its authority; (4) for the three members whose subject is v1's own Rust -- the stage0 mirrors, the lint and the v1 unit tests -- a change to the seed's sources cannot land with the required context green unless a required step judged it, or the seed no longer exists. WHAT THAT MUST BE SUFFICIENT FOR: no member of this population can regress with the required context green. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE THIS ROW, stated because each is the likely mistake: returning any of the four lanes, or any step that hands the corpus to the v1 interpreter, because the ruling withdraws that authority; a native row that judges part of the population, which narrows this row member by member and retires nothing; a manual or dispatched run off the required path; and a count of claims or modules standing where the identity join belongs. The TEMPORARY rung is Mitigatable only while the seed's own runners for these members exist at head, so a change that deletes one of them owes its own declaration."
  }
}
